WEBVTT

00:02.940 --> 00:05.860
Mother, I have something really good to tell you today.

00:06.310 --> 00:08.610
Rita's finally able to talk again!

00:09.150 --> 00:11.740
Ah, I want to hurry up and say "Mother" too.

00:11.820 --> 00:13.450
And be called "Nadja" in return!

00:13.910 --> 00:16.450
We're headed towards the blue Mediterranean Sea, and I love every bit of it!

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

02:27.180 --> 02:29.560
﻿The sea really is nice!

02:30.310 --> 02:31.770
﻿Isn't it. Master?

02:33.190 --> 02:36.530
﻿Yeah, the weather is nice, and the salt is good!

02:36.740 --> 02:40.280
﻿If we keep going at this rate, we'll be in Barcelona the day after tomorrow!

02:40.820 --> 02:41.910
﻿The day after tomorrow?!

02:42.240 --> 02:43.990
﻿Yes, that's right.

02:43.990 --> 02:47.410
﻿When we speak of Spain, we think of the flamenco, don't we?

02:47.410 --> 02:49.410
﻿Viva Flamenco!

02:51.460 --> 02:56.960
﻿But, even so, I don't know if I can make a Flamenco costume before we arrive.

02:57.300 --> 02:59.880
﻿We have a thirteen year old seamstress girl right here.

03:00.510 --> 03:03.390
﻿So, you should be able to do this all by herself!

03:03.430 --> 03:04.680
﻿What?!

03:04.930 --> 03:06.850
﻿All by myself?!

03:11.870 --> 03:16.920
Great Terror! The Ghost Ship of the Mediterranean

03:19.950 --> 03:22.700
﻿Oh! A seagull! Haha, it's so cute!

03:23.870 --> 03:25.620
﻿Look, it's dolphins!

03:29.080 --> 03:31.410
﻿Ah, don't! Creme, Chocolat!

03:31.420 --> 03:34.170
﻿If you fall into the water, you'll drown you know!

03:35.460 --> 03:37.420
﻿At any rate, you sure are talking a lot!

03:37.420 --> 03:38.190
That's a good thing.

03:38.710 --> 03:41.090
﻿It'd be better if she talked even more.

03:41.170 --> 03:44.590
﻿She's probably trying to make up for lost time.

03:44.760 --> 03:47.010
﻿Sylvie, the dolphins are jumping!

03:47.010 --> 03:48.760
﻿Is that right? That's great.

03:48.770 --> 03:52.770
﻿At any rate, if you don't move about like this, you won't get enough exercise!

03:55.270 --> 03:58.110
﻿It's because when we're at sea, we can't really go looking for treasure!

04:05.490 --> 04:07.620
﻿You guys, I wouldn't say anything bad around here!

04:07.830 --> 04:10.490
﻿In this part of the sea, it'd be better if we just stay quiet for now.

04:11.080 --> 04:11.910
﻿How come?

04:12.000 --> 04:13.540
﻿It will appear.

04:13.790 --> 04:15.330
﻿Inside these waters...

04:15.460 --> 04:16.080
﻿Appear?

04:16.630 --> 04:17.500
﻿It will appear.

04:17.790 --> 04:19.250
﻿What's going to appear?

04:19.500 --> 04:21.630
﻿It's obvious! When we say "appear" we mean...

04:21.720 --> 04:22.800
﻿Ghosts!

04:22.840 --> 04:24.590
﻿G-ghosts!!!!!!

04:26.220 --> 04:26.970
﻿Ghosts?

04:27.430 --> 04:29.390
﻿On these seas, it's a renowned story.

04:29.680 --> 04:32.890
﻿So when you pass through here, you'd better hope that you're not found by the ghosts.

04:33.100 --> 04:35.850
﻿If everyone stops talking, we'll be allowed to pass through unharmed.

04:36.020 --> 04:39.230
﻿No way! And if there even is one, I think I'd like to meet it at least once!

04:39.440 --> 04:41.860
HEY!!! Mr. Ghost!!!

04:42.440 --> 04:43.820
﻿Ah, geez!!

04:43.820 --> 04:45.360
﻿Can I really do this all by myself?!

04:45.360 --> 04:46.950
﻿Can I, Can I?!

04:50.740 --> 04:52.160
﻿Geez... what should I do?

04:53.000 --> 04:54.870
﻿About three hundred years ago,

04:55.000 --> 04:57.500
﻿an era where pirates thrived upon the seas was amongst us!

04:58.880 --> 05:02.460
﻿During that time, Spain, England and France were up in flames!

05:05.300 --> 05:08.840
﻿Spain's gold and silver treasures that were being transported from South America...

05:08.850 --> 05:12.520
﻿...were plundered by pirates from countries like England and France!

05:12.850 --> 05:16.770
﻿Within that lot, came the "Castanets", a brave and determined group of pirates.

05:16.900 --> 05:18.770
﻿This group was just a little bit famous.

05:42.090 --> 05:44.920
﻿They were a group of pirates that made it difficult to be able to deliver the goods, but...

05:45.260 --> 05:48.630
﻿In a grand battle with the invincible Spanish armada,

05:49.010 --> 05:50.510
﻿they were destroyed.

05:56.640 --> 05:58.640
﻿The phantom ship of that group of pirates,

05:58.850 --> 06:02.310
﻿is even now still wandering about these waters.

06:02.730 --> 06:04.360
﻿The phantom ship!

06:06.150 --> 06:09.030
﻿Once you realize you're up against the phantom ship, it's all over.

06:09.200 --> 06:10.740
O-O-O-Once you've realized it...

06:11.240 --> 06:12.740
﻿Your ship's engine will stop.

06:12.740 --> 06:14.120
﻿And as you stir about in panic..

06:14.120 --> 06:14.910
and ﻿as you stir about in panic...

06:14.910 --> 06:18.460
﻿The phantom ship will appear in midst of the fog and all of the crew aboard...

06:18.790 --> 06:20.920
﻿...will end up cursed and die a horrible death!!

06:21.040 --> 06:22.880
﻿C-Cursed and die a horrible death?!

06:23.340 --> 06:27.630
﻿So until we leave this area, it's better if we keep our voices down and try to stay quiet.

06:27.630 --> 06:30.180
﻿So while we ride on this ship, please try to keep all talk down to a whisper.

06:30.430 --> 06:32.300
﻿How's that? Pretty scary, isn't it?

06:33.640 --> 06:34.560
﻿Not at all!

06:35.560 --> 06:37.310
﻿It's probably all just superstition, right

06:39.440 --> 06:41.190
﻿Th-Th-Th-That's right!!

06:41.350 --> 06:43.980
﻿I-If we believe that it's just superstition, there's no reason to be scare—

06:52.490 --> 06:54.490
﻿First of all, I need to prepare all of the tools...

06:54.740 --> 06:58.250
﻿With scissors, a tape measure, that roll!

07:00.500 --> 07:02.120
﻿Oh... an ill omen..

07:02.580 --> 07:04.590
﻿Oh, it's just you Granny.

07:04.880 --> 07:06.210
﻿What's the ill omen?

07:06.670 --> 07:07.960
﻿I'm not sure...

07:08.670 --> 07:11.880
﻿But my crystal ball has been very active since a while ago.

07:12.180 --> 07:15.930
﻿Maybe it's a sign that some sort of calamity is about to befall upon this ship.

07:16.140 --> 07:17.390
﻿Could it be that...?!

07:17.600 --> 07:18.810
﻿What are you talking about?

07:18.810 --> 07:22.140
﻿Even on the slim chance that the phantom ship appears, all of us aboard the ship,

07:22.150 --> 07:24.020
We will easily hold our own!

07:24.020 --> 07:25.520
So don't you worry.

07:28.190 --> 07:29.650
﻿Phantom ship...

07:30.070 --> 07:32.150
﻿Could it be that... you're scared?

07:32.860 --> 07:34.450
﻿No... No way!

07:34.910 --> 07:38.700
﻿The phantom ship may be scary, but we traveling performers can manage for sure!!

07:38.700 --> 07:43.580
﻿A-And a-also, to talk about pirates in th-this day and age...

07:43.580 --> 07:47.000
﻿That's right! There's no way pirates would exist in this day and age.

07:47.170 --> 07:49.300
﻿But, there may be ghosts.

07:52.050 --> 07:52.970
﻿An ill omen...

07:54.720 --> 07:57.180
﻿The scariest thing is Granny's face.

07:58.890 --> 08:00.640
﻿There's no point in being afraid of it.

08:01.180 --> 08:02.560
﻿I have to try at least!

08:15.780 --> 08:17.660
﻿My goodness, isn't this sloppy...

08:17.660 --> 08:19.200
﻿In the middle of the day like this...

08:19.200 --> 08:21.250
﻿There's no way a ghost would come out.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.370
﻿Hey, Master, aren't you drinking a little too much?

08:24.540 --> 08:25.750
﻿What's that?

08:26.000 --> 08:29.250
﻿You're scared of the ghost ship, so you call on the Master to take care of it, eh?

08:30.840 --> 08:32.260
So you're scared after all!

08:32.670 --> 08:33.470
﻿This is an ill omen!

08:37.550 --> 08:38.470
﻿I...

08:39.600 --> 08:41.970
﻿Just what's going on here?

08:42.850 --> 08:44.350
﻿The ship is stopping!

08:52.940 --> 08:54.820
﻿Huh? It stopped!

08:55.570 --> 08:57.240
﻿What happened?

09:02.540 --> 09:04.250
﻿Th-Th-Th-Th-There no way this could be...

09:04.250 --> 09:05.870
﻿F-F-F-F-F-F-F-F-Fog!!!

09:05.870 --> 09:07.500
﻿F-F-F-F-F-F-F-F-Fog!!!

09:07.500 --> 09:09.330
﻿Hey, don't say stuff like that...

09:09.340 --> 09:11.800
﻿Th-Th-This really is...!

09:12.050 --> 09:14.170
﻿"The boat will stop and the fog will appear..."

09:14.300 --> 09:15.970
﻿It's just like what we were talking about before.

09:16.130 --> 09:17.970
﻿D-D-Don't be absurd!

09:17.970 --> 09:19.680
﻿Don't try to scare me!

09:20.350 --> 09:20.890
﻿But...

09:21.600 --> 09:22.470
﻿But?!

09:22.560 --> 09:23.310
﻿Over there...

09:42.330 --> 09:44.700
﻿It's appeared!!!!

09:45.580 --> 09:46.540
﻿Ah, there it is, there it is.

09:47.330 --> 09:49.170
﻿It looks like all of the threads got tied up together.

10:21.370 --> 10:24.540
﻿Th-Th-There's no way a phantom ship would... really...

10:24.740 --> 10:26.620
﻿B-B-B-But... we'll be fine...!

10:26.620 --> 10:29.790
﻿Wove got really strong, powerful people aboard this ship...!

10:29.790 --> 10:32.420
﻿Aaaahhh! It really appeared!

10:32.840 --> 10:34.000
﻿Hey, hey!

10:35.260 --> 10:36.670
﻿First do this...

10:43.260 --> 10:45.390
﻿Hey, there are still people here!

10:45.390 --> 10:46.600
﻿Open this up!

10:47.520 --> 10:48.810
﻿Open up!

10:51.480 --> 10:53.190
﻿Open up, open up, open up!

10:53.190 --> 10:54.480
﻿Wait a minute!
Open up, open up, open up!

10:55.020 --> 10:56.480
﻿That's a fake.

10:56.480 --> 10:57.990
﻿A-A fake?

10:57.990 --> 11:00.610
﻿That ship does look like a phantom ship, but...

11:00.740 --> 11:02.490
﻿There's smoke coming out of the ship's smokestack.

11:02.740 --> 11:04.780
﻿Also, on the side of the boat,

11:05.030 --> 11:07.580
﻿there are a lot of white fumes coming out.

11:08.120 --> 11:10.580
﻿That ship is the newest style steamship.

11:10.830 --> 11:13.710
﻿This fog also looks like something that was artificially made.

11:13.880 --> 11:16.920
﻿So you're saying that they're some sort of upper class ghosts?

11:16.920 --> 11:17.880
﻿Wrong, dummy.

11:17.880 --> 11:19.090
﻿Then, what is it?

11:19.170 --> 11:22.550
﻿They're trying to take advantage of the superstitious people

11:22.550 --> 11:24.260
﻿who ride ships and are afraid of ghost stories.

11:24.550 --> 11:27.850
﻿And it probably wasn't a coincidence that the engine stopped.

11:28.060 --> 11:28.930
That ﻿means...!

11:29.520 --> 11:32.140
﻿They're probably the ones that stopped the engine.

11:32.730 --> 11:34.940
﻿They're getting in contact with their comrades.

11:35.320 --> 11:36.900
﻿You finally get it, right?

11:36.940 --> 11:39.190
﻿There's no way that's a phantom ship.

11:39.190 --> 11:42.240
﻿They're just ordinary pirates disguised as ghosts!

12:30.120 --> 12:31.830
﻿Take a look, we re right after all.

12:31.830 --> 12:33.660
﻿I see. I should have known it was like that.

12:34.540 --> 12:36.880
I ﻿see. I should have known it was like that.

12:38.320 --> 12:39.150
Wait a minute!

12:39.800 --> 12:43.220
﻿So you're saying that they're not ghosts, but humans?!

12:43.220 --> 12:44.880
﻿That's what we've been saying all along.

12:44.880 --> 12:46.130
﻿Aah! I can't forgive them!

12:46.800 --> 12:49.430
﻿Trying to totally scare all of us grown-ups

12:49.430 --> 12:52.560
﻿I, the Great One, will hunt them down and punish them!

12:54.890 --> 12:56.560
﻿So you were scared after all.

12:57.150 --> 12:58.730
﻿But, you can relax now.

12:58.730 --> 13:01.980
﻿Once the Master gets serious, you better come prepared with arrows and guns.

13:07.450 --> 13:08.910
﻿Granny, watch out!

13:10.540 --> 13:11.330
﻿How annoying!

13:26.880 --> 13:29.090
﻿Take that!

13:30.260 --> 13:31.760
﻿On with the plan!

13:35.810 --> 13:37.560
﻿The trick to the sewing machine is smooth motions!

13:42.530 --> 13:45.280
﻿Damn it! These guys plan on boarding this ship!

13:45.280 --> 13:48.660
﻿Hey, don't you worry. We'll send them packing, and there won't be anyone left!

13:51.830 --> 13:54.830
﻿Thomas! You should stand tall and fight too!

13:54.830 --> 13:55.660
﻿No way, no way, no way!

13:55.960 --> 13:59.170
﻿I hate ghosts, but I hate violence even more!

13:59.170 --> 14:00.580
﻿Is this the time to be saying something like that?

14:00.590 --> 14:01.500
﻿I'm really sorry!

14:01.500 --> 14:02.500
﻿Thomas!

14:02.500 --> 14:05.420
﻿I already told you! This isn't what my body was made for! I'm weak!!

14:05.420 --> 14:06.630
﻿Geez...

14:15.140 --> 14:16.770
﻿Smooth movement, smooth movement...!

14:19.270 --> 14:21.270
﻿To start with, take control of the ship's bridge!

14:22.230 --> 14:23.610
﻿Wait a minute!

14:27.990 --> 14:29.110
﻿Wh-What's this?

14:29.450 --> 14:33.280
﻿You guys really didn't think you'll get away with doing something like this, did you?

14:33.910 --> 14:36.540
If you go home quietly, we'll overlook it this time.

14:36.790 --> 14:38.160
Hurry up and go home!

14:41.500 --> 14:43.290
Just ﻿what are you guys?!

14:43.630 --> 14:44.630
﻿I'll sound the foghorn!

14:44.920 --> 14:48.920
﻿We re an unshakable group that takes on the world's challenges. The Dandelion Troupe!

14:51.430 --> 14:52.510
﻿I'm finally finished!

14:57.390 --> 14:58.890
﻿What's wrong, Master?

15:05.150 --> 15:06.860
Oh dear... is he seasick?

15:15.330 --> 15:16.410
﻿That's impossible.

15:19.540 --> 15:20.710
﻿Master!

15:20.710 --> 15:22.790
That's why I said you were drinking too much.

15:27.260 --> 15:28.420
﻿How stupid!

15:28.420 --> 15:30.130
﻿Some idiotic traveling performers.

15:30.130 --> 15:32.590
﻿Do you think you can match us pirates?

15:32.840 --> 15:33.720
﻿Let's do this!

15:36.470 --> 15:38.470
﻿I hate violence!

15:46.820 --> 15:48.400
Relax. I hit you the flat side of my blade!

15:51.990 --> 15:53.410
Creme! Chocolat!

16:00.290 --> 16:03.750
﻿A-Ah! J-Just wait! Could you hold this for me?

16:04.540 --> 16:05.580
﻿Thanks.

16:06.880 --> 16:08.300
﻿Hey, I'm busy over here!

16:08.300 --> 16:09.420
﻿Hurry up and do it!

16:09.420 --> 16:09.920
﻿Yes, sir.

16:10.340 --> 16:11.630
﻿Come on!

16:12.840 --> 16:13.800
﻿W-Why you!

16:17.100 --> 16:19.810
﻿Here, take that, that, and that!

16:37.200 --> 16:37.820
﻿We did it!

16:38.160 --> 16:39.990
﻿What are you doing?

16:39.990 --> 16:41.910
﻿There's only five of them at the most!

16:41.910 --> 16:45.290
﻿No, but... these guys are pretty tough.

16:45.290 --> 16:47.460
﻿Move and fight using the difference in numbers!

16:47.590 --> 16:49.670
﻿Don't just play with them!

16:52.920 --> 16:55.680
﻿As expected, it's pretty difficult with this number...

16:57.140 --> 16:59.050
﻿What should I do here?

17:04.810 --> 17:07.310
﻿How about you guys give up soon?

17:08.480 --> 17:11.360
﻿It seems like we can't be indecisive about our strategy anymore.

17:11.980 --> 17:14.400
﻿It might be dangerous, but I'll use that.

17:15.320 --> 17:17.160
﻿You aren't seriously thinking of using that, are you?

17:17.320 --> 17:19.370
﻿There's no other way left.

17:19.490 --> 17:20.740
It's dangerous. It'd be better if you don't.

17:21.200 --> 17:23.040
﻿If we won't be able to return home if they take the ship, will we?

17:23.250 --> 17:24.160
But...

17:24.160 --> 17:25.500
Ill omen!

17:25.580 --> 17:27.080
﻿Rita, the usual thing.

17:27.080 --> 17:27.750
﻿Okay!

17:28.080 --> 17:28.770
﻿Abel.

17:28.770 --> 17:29.360
Yeah.

17:29.540 --> 17:31.250
﻿Thomas, we're counting on you.

17:31.250 --> 17:32.550
﻿We won't let you!
Ah, wait!

17:44.060 --> 17:46.350
﻿Okay, Thomas! Give it everything you've got!

17:46.520 --> 17:48.810
﻿Why me!?

17:50.310 --> 17:51.400
﻿What the...?

17:51.400 --> 17:53.070
﻿Drunken style martial arts.

17:55.400 --> 17:57.900
﻿Wha-Wha... What's going on here?!

17:58.160 --> 18:00.120
﻿Now, we re going to fight too!

18:20.760 --> 18:22.180
﻿No way!

18:22.180 --> 18:22.800
﻿We can do this.

18:22.810 --> 18:23.930
﻿If it continues like this, we're going to win.

18:25.730 --> 18:26.470
﻿That's as far as you go.

18:27.940 --> 18:28.560
﻿Granny!

18:31.270 --> 18:32.360
﻿You better not make any strange movements,

18:32.360 --> 18:35.780
﻿Otherwise, this hostage's life will come to a very quick end.

18:41.280 --> 18:42.490
﻿Now, throw down your weapons!

18:42.990 --> 18:44.160
It's gone this far, huh?

18:44.330 --> 18:45.410
If you want to go at it...

18:45.750 --> 18:47.160
﻿Go ahead and try!

18:47.160 --> 18:48.370
﻿E-Everyone!

18:48.660 --> 18:49.540
﻿What was that?

18:49.750 --> 18:52.670
﻿Okay, everyone! Clean up the rest!

18:56.840 --> 18:57.710
﻿Take this!

19:00.010 --> 19:02.220
﻿Uh.. Umm... What's going on?

19:03.800 --> 19:05.470
﻿Uhh... Chief...

19:05.850 --> 19:08.100
A-Ah... ﻿What... What's with these guys?

19:08.100 --> 19:10.730
﻿Don't they understand what the word hostage means?!

19:11.150 --> 19:13.310
﻿If it's going to be like this, I'll at least kill this one....

19:13.310 --> 19:16.610
﻿All right! Die!

19:20.610 --> 19:22.160
﻿Wh-Where?

19:22.410 --> 19:24.700
﻿Huh? Where could it have gone?

19:28.080 --> 19:29.250
﻿Here it is, here it is!

19:37.130 --> 19:42.470
Oh, ugh, oh, hey, he... Wait, wait!

19:43.300 --> 19:46.140
﻿Ya-Ya-Ya.. Don't do that! Hyo-hyo-yo...

19:46.430 --> 19:49.810
﻿Kill them! No matter what they do, kill them!!

19:53.980 --> 19:55.150
Thank you.

19:56.230 --> 20:00.990
Ah, no, uhhh... I wonder if I'm in some bad dream.

20:02.740 --> 20:03.820
That's why I said it...

20:04.530 --> 20:06.070
﻿Go ahead and try it!

20:07.410 --> 20:09.240
﻿Master!!

20:09.620 --> 20:12.330
﻿Hey, everyone. Sorry to make you wait.

